<title>USA: PP&amp;L pushes back Susquehanna 1 nuke restart.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L pushes back Susquehanna 1 nuke restart.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power &amp; Light Co pushed back the restart of its 1,090 megawatt (MW) Susquehanna 1 nuclear power plant to Tuesday, a company spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;They expect to be on line tomorrow,&quot; the spokesman said, adding the company needed more time to repair a safety relief valve.</p>
<p>PP&amp;L expected to startup the Berwick, Pa., unit midday Sunday from a scheduled maintenance and refueling outage that began September 7.</p>
<p>The Susquehanna plant is jointly owned by PP&amp;L and Allegheny Electric Cooperative Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
